<title>BELGIUM: Sugar panel to discuss MFN imports.</title>
<headline>Sugar panel to discuss MFN imports.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's sugar management committee will on Wednesday discuss a most-favoured-nation (MFN) raw cane sugar import quota for 1997, EU member state officials said.</p>
<p>The quota, amounting to some 22,000 tonnes of white sugar equivalent, compensates Finland's traditional suppliers under the former General Agreement on Tariffs and Trade (GATT) for trade losses after it joined the EU in 1995.</p>
<p>It benefits suppliers such as Cuba and Brazil.</p>
<p>The sugar panel will also discuss sugar supplies for remote regions, the officials said.</p>
<p>The discussion will cover supplies to the Azores, Canary Islands and Aegean islands.</p>
<p>Decisions on the MFN and remote region supply arrangements are expected next week.</p>
</text>
